{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And he answered</b> — this angel [answered] to those standing before this angel, and he is prince over them, for they do whatever he commands them. Some say: for before him refers back to Joshua. This is far-fetched, for why would men stand before him, and what superiority does he have because he is clothed in filthy garments? Know that לבוש is a transitive participle (פועל יוצא), and when he says לובש he dons himself, and לבוש is another [thing] placed upon him — these filthy garments. And the word עונך is like גדול עוני מנשוא — נשוא [means] great is my punishment and my suffering; therefore he says after it: הן גרשת אותי וגם זה עונך ככה." "<b>I have removed from upon you</b> — your punishment and your suffering and your shame, in the manner of ונקה האיש מעון. And likewise: והאשה תשא את עונה." "<b>מחלצות</b> — like את חליצתו — חליפתו, something that is removed from him. And מחלצות — garments with which others change in place of them."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {0 "The second נשוא in the phrase גדול עוני מנשוא is translated as if parsing it as a noun (greatness), following the context of Ibn Ezra's argument; alternatively it could be rendered literally as 'borne,' but the argument about עון meaning punishment supports the gloss given."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:45:53.931210895Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}